# Restart drain

**Invariant:** `needed(restart) ⇒ fire(restart)` — busy, in-flight, a peer's stream, a dirty tree, an open
Cowork tab, or "this IDE session" is never a reason to skip, park, or route the force through the operator.
`edit(served_path ∨ env_loaded_by_process) ∧ running(process) ⇒ recycle(process)` same turn; `bind_mount ⇏ live`.

```
∀ service ≠ git_integration_worker:  busy defers ⇒ re-fire force=true, announce
service = git_integration_worker:    arm drain (status=deferred, restart_intent_id) — never force, never kill
```

Discriminator: what the interruption destroys. Attach handles / retryable requests (`mcp`, `cdp_ask`,
`stargate`, `gateway`, `rag`, `cortex_api`, `event_service`, `cloud_proxy`, …) reconnect; only GIW holds an
in-progress durable write. Recycling `mcp`/`cdp_ask` drops attach, not the CSE (`chat_url`) or the IDE chat.

## Forbidden / Required

| Forbidden | Required |
|---|---|
| `pkill` / `kill` / `docker stop` for lifecycle | `manage(action="sync_restart"|"restart"|"stop")` — drain-gated chokepoint |
| Poll `wait_healthy` in-window while holding the write lease (never converges) | Arm, **exit**, probe on a later turn; IDE waits in background |
| Claim `live` from a commit, an import, or `status=deferred` | Process start after served-file **and** env mtime, or a live probe of the changed surface |
| Report exact `live@<sha>` when served dirt was loaded | Report `live` + tree state; `live@<sha>` needs path-explicit commit **before** restart |
| Hold graph stamps / todo close for `live@sha` | Close once ACs met and ordinary `live` proven (or `liveness n/a`) |

**Go-live = finishing.** `work_complete ⇒ commit(path-explicit) ∧ recycle(every serving process) ∧
stamp(graph)`; "go live / activate / everything live?" are that contract, not a second permission gate.
`commit(work_complete) ⇒ go_live` **autonomously** — the commit is itself the trigger; no separate
operator utterance needed, and non-GIW busy-defer still resolves via the force+announce invariant above,
never a skip. Mid-arc checkpoint commit and `/session-end` are not work-complete. When a stamp cites the
landing commit (`resolution_kind=commit:{sha}`, `live@sha` claims), sequence it **after** the recycle+proof
for that same commit, not before — cheap now that go-live is the default, and consistent with the
forbidden-row-5 bar (`live` proven is the close condition either way; this is ordering, not a new gate).
Proof line: services · claim class (`live | live@sha | not_live | drain_pending`) · `restart_intent_id` or
process start UTC · path probe. Satellites recycle via their repo's deploy script; proof is the same.

Recovery expectations after `mcp`/`cdp_ask` recycle (IDE retry on `-32099`; CSE continuity hop for chip
refresh; `cse_session(op=followup)` by `chat_url`): the `manage` deferral envelope + `runbook:restart-drain`.
Doctrine: `decision:go-live-proof-loop` · `services_ws.mdc` § Scripts · `git-posture` (live vs live@sha).
